From afc0763426a683065827968f8bed8f742f261d14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:17:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/34] vulkan: decode conv step in one dispatch; skip list for
 nodes an earlier dispatch already did

CONCAT(conv state, x^T) -> SSM_CONV -> SILU and the CPY of the shifted window back over the state (an identity
view of the cache row) run as one conv_step dispatch at the CONCAT (-96 launches per Bonsai decode token; same
arithmetic as ssm_conv.comp). build_graph returns early for listed nodes, so they cost neither a dispatch nor a
barrier; the dispatch that did their work records what it wrote. Never the last computed node. The GDN in-place
CPY uses the list too. GGML_VK_DISABLE_CONV_STEP turns it off. Test: CONV_STEP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
